  "sources": [
    "https://assets.nexperia.com/documents/data-sheet/74HC_HCT14.pdf"
  ],
  "model_notes": [
    "Own behavioral implementation, calibrated to selected datasheet points; no vendor SPICE copied.",
    "Finite asymmetric output resistance, input DC current/capacitance, per-output source/sink current warnings and powered propagation delays are represented.",
    "Output current ratings trigger warnings, not artificial hard current clamps. No transistor-level short-circuit or protection model.",
    "Delay, drive strength and consumption use nominal values near the stated reference supply; full supply-dependent timing/drive curves, damage, input clamp/back-powering and temperature are outside this model. Inputs without an external driver remain unknown.",
    "Reference: 4.5 V. Typical VT+=2.38 V and VT-=1.4 V; fixed ratios scale approximately at other supplies (not a full threshold curve).",
    "Source/sink resistances 45/37.5 ohm fit typical 4 mA drive points at 4.5 V; current warnings use 4 mA reference ratings. CPD=7 pF per switching input; IQ=1 uA illustrative nominal.",
    "11 ns internal delay plus 2 ns code transition and load RC approximate 12 ns propagation at 5 V/15 pF. Internal CMOS dynamic ICC=CPD*VCC*f; slow-ramp excess ICC is not included.",
    "Schmitt inputs retain the last valid level between thresholds; initial in-band inputs are unknown. Loss of supply or external drive invalidates the retained input state.",
    "Per-output current warnings use a first-order 1 us averaging window for DC operating ratings; normal short capacitive charging peaks are not instantaneous overload limits."
  ],
  "measurement_ports": {
    "positive": "vcc",
    "negative": "gnd"
  },
  "category": "Digital/Logic ICs",
  "family": "74HC"
}
